{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.72,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["GND", "Display_Power_Switch"],
      "observed": "C1 is implemented as 0.1 uF / 16 V on the EPD power/boost input node.",
      "expected": "The specification states that Meshinger C1 should be 1 uF / 25 V, matching C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 in the PDI reference implementation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C1\") (value \"0.1uF/16V\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The EPD driver/boost input has roughly one tenth of the intended capacitance and a lower voltage rating than specified, increasing rail ripple and potentially causing unstable EPD power or boost-converter operation.",
      "confidence": 0.72
    },
    {
      "category": "footprint_mismatch",
      "components": ["C11"],
      "pins": ["C11.1", "C11.2"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(C11-Pad1)", "GND"],
      "observed": "C11 is a 0.1 uF capacitor placed in an Inductor_SMD footprint, and its pin 1 is left unconnected.",
      "expected": "A capacitor should use a capacitor footprint and, if populated, be connected to a meaningful net; otherwise it should be omitted or marked DNP. The specification does not describe a floating capacitor in this position.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C11\") (value \"0.1uF\") (footprint \"Inductor_SMD:L_0805_2012Metric_Pad1.05x1.20mm_HandSolder\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"59\") (name \"unconnected-(C11-Pad1)\")"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Likely benign if the part is unpopulated, but if assembled it indicates a wrong part/footprint or a missing bypass connection rather than the intended power-section filtering.",
      "confidence": 0.4
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The main anomaly is C1 in the EPD driver being 0.1 uF/16 V instead of the specified 1 uF/25 V, which reduces intended EPD power-rail decoupling. A secondary suspicious issue is C11, a floating capacitor placed in an inductor footprint."
}

